{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KjkV9pyj5o9QjjTNjENSwK","type":"tool_result","content":"100\t      - R2.6:\n101\t          text: |\n102\t            Must set LC_ALL=C in the environment for both binaries unless the DiffTest.Env\n103\t            explicitly overrides LC_ALL. This ensures deterministic sort order and formatting\n104\t            across locales. The harness applies this default before merging DiffTest.Env.\n105\t\n106\t  R3:\n107\t    title: Comparison and reporting\n108\t    items:\n109\t      - R3.1:\n110\t          text: Must apply the DiffTest.Normalize function (if non-nil) to both binaries' stdout and stderr before comparison.\n111\t      - R3.2:\n112\t          text: Must compare normalized stdout byte-for-byte. Any difference must be reported as a test failure.\n113\t      - R3.3:\n114\t          text: Must compare normalized stderr byte-for-byte. Any difference must be reported as a test failure.\n115\t      - R3.4:\n116\t          text: Must compare exit codes exactly. A difference must be reported as a test failure.\n117\t      - R3.5:\n118\t          text: 'Must report divergence with the following information in the failure message: the DiffTest args, the stdin content (truncated to 256 bytes if longer), the reference binary stdout, the Go binary stdout, the reference stderr, the Go stderr, and both exit codes.'\n119\t      - R3.6:\n120\t          text: Must run each DiffTest as a named subtest (t.Run) so individual test case failures are identifiable in go test output.\n121\t\n122\t  R4:\n123\t    title: Normalization hooks\n124\t    items:\n125\t      - R4.1:\n126\t          text: Must allow per-DiffTest normalization via the Normalize field. The function receives the raw output bytes and returns the normalized bytes.\n127\t      - R4.2:\n128\t          text: Must provide a built-in TimestampNormalizer that replaces common strftime timestamp patterns with a fixed placeholder string. This normalizer is used by cmd/ts tests.\n129\t      - R4.3:\n130\t          text: |\n131\t            Must allow normalizers to be composed: the harness must accept a slice of Normalize\n132\t            functions applied in order, not a single function. When the slice is nil or empty,\n133\t            no normalization is applied.\n134\t      - R4.4:\n135\t          text: |\n136\t            Must provide func ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc that returns\n137\t            a single NormalizeFunc applying the given functions in order. This is a convenience\n138\t            for cmd/ test files that combine multiple normalizers:\n139\t\n140\t              normalize := testutils.ComposeNormalizers(\n141\t                  testutils.TimestampNormalizer,\n142\t                  customNormalizer,\n143\t              )\n144\t\n145\t  R5:\n146\t    title: File-state comparison\n147\t    items:\n148\t      - R5.1:\n149\t          text: |\n150\t            Must support utilities whose primary output is a file rather than stdout (sponge,\n151\t            cp, mv). DiffTest.ExpectedFiles is a map[string][]byte where keys are file paths\n152\t            relative to the working directory and values are the expected byte content after\n153\t            execution. When ExpectedFiles is non-nil, the harness checks each entry after both\n154\t            binaries complete.\n155\t      - R5.2:\n156\t          text: |\n157\t            Must compare each ExpectedFiles entry byte-for-byte against the file produced by\n158\t            the Go binary. Any difference must be reported as a test failure with the same\n159\t            format as stdout divergence: file path, expected content (from reference), actual\n160\t            content (from Go binary). Missing files must also be reported as failures.\n161\t\n162\tnon_goals:\n163\t  - pkg/testutils does not build or compile the Go binaries under test.\n164\t  - pkg/testutils does not install or manage Homebrew reference binaries.\n165\t  - pkg/testutils does not produce test reports beyond standard go test output.\n166\t  - pkg/testutils does not implement retry logic; a failing test fails immediately.\n167\t  - pkg/testutils does not mock or stub the filesystem or OS for unit testing cmd/ packages.\n168\t\n169\tpackage_contract:\n170\t  exports:\n171\t    - name: DiffTest\n172\t      signature: \"type DiffTest struct { Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; Normalize []NormalizeFunc; ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte }\"\n173\t    - name: NormalizeFunc\n174\t      signature: \"type NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte\"\n175\t    - name: RunDiffTests\n176\t      signature: \"func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\"\n177\t    - name: ComposeNormalizers\n178\t      signature: \"func ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc\"\n179\t    - name: TimestampNormalizer\n180\t      signature: \"var TimestampNormalizer NormalizeFunc\"\n181\t  imports:\n182\t    - testing\n183\t    - os\n184\t    - os/exec\n185\t  import_constraints:\n186\t    - \"Must not import any cmd/ package.\"\n187\t    - \"Must not import any other pkg/ package.\"\n188\t\n189\tacceptance_criteria:\n190\t  - id: AC1\n191\t    criterion: \"A cmd/ package can define a []DiffTest slice and call RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) from a TestXxx function with no other setup. RunDiffTests runs each DiffTest as a named subtest (t.Run(test.Name, ...)) and calls t.Fatal on the first divergence in any subtest.\"\n192\t    traces:\n193\t      - R1.1\n194\t      - R1.2\n195\t      - R1.3\n196\t      - R1.4\n197\t  - id: AC2\n198\t    criterion: \"A passing test run produces no output. A failing test prints the triggering args, stdin, and both binaries' stdout, stderr, and exit code.\"\n199\t    traces:"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"27cb1b87-3737-4ae9-82ca-0e3c8c4207df","uuid":"a0ddf27e-26cf